# MCP Venus OS - Example Claude Desktop Configuration

This file shows how to configure the MCP Venus OS server in Claude Desktop.

## Location

The config file is typically at:
- macOS: `~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json`
- Windows: `%APPDATA%\Claude\claude_desktop_config.json`
- Linux: `~/.config/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json`

## Configuration

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "venus-os": {
      "command": "uv",
      "args": [
        "--directory",
        "/Users/vmedvedev/victron/mcp-venus-os",
        "run",
        "mcp-venus-os"
      ],
      "env": {
        "DBUS_BUS_TYPE": "system",
        "DBUS_SERVICE_NAME": "com.victronenergy",
        "MQTT_HOST": "localhost",
        "MQTT_PORT": "1883",
        "MQTT_BASE_TOPIC": "N/venus-os",
        "SAFETY_REQUIRE_CONFIRMATION": "true",
        "SAFETY_MAX_CHARGE_CURRENT": "100",
        "SAFETY_MAX_DISCHARGE_CURRENT": "100",
        "SAFETY_MIN_SOC_LIMIT": "10",
        "SAFETY_MAX_SOC_LIMIT": "100",
        "SAFETY_ALLOWED_MODES": "on,off,charger_only,inverter_only,eco"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Alternative: Using pip install

If you install the package globally:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "venus-os": {
      "command": "mcp-venus-os",
      "env": {
        "DBUS_BUS_TYPE": "system",
        "MQTT_HOST": "localhost",
        "MQTT_PORT": "1883"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Environment Variables

| Variable | Default | Description |
|----------|---------|-------------|
| `DBUS_BUS_TYPE` | `system` | D-Bus type: `system` or `session` |
| `DBUS_SERVICE_NAME` | `com.victronenergy` | Base Victron service name |
| `MQTT_HOST` | `localhost` | MQTT broker hostname |
| `MQTT_PORT` | `1883` | MQTT broker port |
| `MQTT_USERNAME` | - | MQTT username (optional) |
| `MQTT_PASSWORD` | - | MQTT password (optional) |
| `MQTT_CLIENT_ID` | `mcp-venus-os` | MQTT client ID |
| `MQTT_BASE_TOPIC` | `N/venus-os` | Base topic for Venus OS data |
| `MQTT_TLS` | `false` | Use TLS for MQTT |
| `SAFETY_REQUIRE_CONFIRMATION` | `true` | Require confirmation for writes |
| `SAFETY_MAX_CHARGE_CURRENT` | `100` | Max charge current (A) |
| `SAFETY_MAX_DISCHARGE_CURRENT` | `100` | Max discharge current (A) |
| `SAFETY_MIN_SOC_LIMIT` | `10` | Min SoC limit (%) |
| `SAFETY_MAX_SOC_LIMIT` | `100` | Max SoC limit (%) |
| `SAFETY_ALLOWED_MODES` | `on,off,charger_only,inverter_only,eco` | Allowed inverter modes |